Hi team — quick update: I’ve created the 11 Gold App tables for the Media Intelligence Platform across Overview, Breakouts, Crosstabs, and Explore:
- sdi_tbl_mip_gold_appOverviewCards_wide
- sdi_tbl_mip_gold_appOverviewTrend_long
- sdi_tbl_mip_gold_appOverviewToplineMovers_long
- sdi_tbl_mip_gold_appOverviewConversionFunnel_long
- sdi_tbl_mip_gold_appBreakoutsComparisonTable_long
- sdi_tbl_mip_gold_appBreakoutsWaterfall_long
- sdi_tbl_mip_gold_appBreakoutsAbsoluteTrend_long
- sdi_tbl_mip_gold_appCrosstabsMatrix_long
- sdi_tbl_mip_gold_appCrosstabsRankedPairs_long
- sdi_tbl_mip_gold_appExploreBase_wide
- sdi_tbl_mip_gold_appExploreRankedPairs_long
These tables are designed as the application-ready layer for the backend/API and include the relevant combinations needed by each section, such as reporting week, LOB/platform context, metric, comparison type (Prior week, 4-wk trend, Same wk LY), display-size logic, breakout dimensions, crosstab pairings, rankings, and other UI-facing values where applicable.

This is still under active refinement as we continue iterating on the UI, API requirements, naming, and overall user experience. I’m continuing to simplify the schemas, remove unnecessary fields, and align each table more closely with what the corresponding application section actually needs.



SELECT
    targetWeekStartDate,
    filterLob,
    filterPlatform,
    metricName,
    pairKey,
    comparisonType,
    displaySize,
    rowBreakoutValue,
    columnBreakoutValue,
    COUNT(*) AS rowCount
FROM prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_tbl_mip_gold_appCrosstabsMatrix_long
GROUP BY
    targetWeekStartDate,
    filterLob,
    filterPlatform,
    metricName,
    pairKey,
    comparisonType,
    displaySize,
    rowBreakoutValue,
    columnBreakoutValue
HAVING COUNT(*)>1
ORDER BY rowCount DESC;

SELECT
    targetWeekStartDate,
    comparisonType,
    displaySize,
    COUNT(*) AS rows,
    COUNT(DISTINCT metricName) AS metrics,
    COUNT(DISTINCT pairKey) AS orientedPairs
FROM prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_tbl_mip_gold_appCrosstabsMatrix_long
GROUP BY targetWeekStartDate,comparisonType,displaySize
ORDER BY targetWeekStartDate,comparisonType,displaySize;
